elf  i was what  eight years old then i thought if i  could just become invisible that would  be even better  but crystal night itself  my father fortunately had come home from  work  and he had a very good job at the  stationary firm  and we sat on the floor in our apartment  in the dark  and we were told not to make a sound she  didn't want the neighbors to know that  we were home  and we could have the screaming and the  yelling outside  and and uh people looking for jews and  yelling saying you know kill the jews  and all that  and that made an impression you know  i can't even imagine no and then  we we we stayed home for a day or so  after that  and then we went out and we saw all the  our synagogue wasn't  in all ashes you know they had burned it  down  and there was so much glass on the  street  and they they had jewish people come out  with their toothbrushes i'm not making  this up and had them kneel on the street  and scrub the street while people  were around there jeering at them  fortunately when we got to  shanghai there were there was help by  refugee organizations  american organizations and and the art  people you know and and  also some local russian jews helped  and then came world war ii and it was  all over again  then the japanese were in charge then  the japanese they were right there  all the time and then they took over and  if you had been an american  or a british or a dutch citizen they  would have put you in a detention camp  and that was very bad  it wasn't like a concentration camp but  it was close  they didn't kill you in there but there  was no food not enough food and  hygiene you weren't allowed to leave at  that point right oh no no no no  where would we go we had no papers  we had we were stuck there and then they  they looked around the japanese looked  around and  saw all these uh refugees german  refugees  jewish refugees and they didn't know  what to do with us  because we're kind of in a gray zone  there you know  and so t